If one assumes spatial (or spatial-temporal) correlation a
priori based on the field sampling design and fits an INLA model with spatial (or
spatial-temporal) correlation accordingly, is there anything wrong with using
this model versus one without the correlation structure if the former doesn’t improve
(reduce) the DIC/WAIC by at least 10 points or so relative to the latter? Thank
you.

