One nice way to think of splines, is that it is a non-parametric correction to a
linear effect.

To get this, you need to add the linear effect and remove it from the spline,
but adding extraconstr saying that (1:m)^T %*% spline = 0

I made a small example to illustrate

Best
Havard

On Wed, 2025-09-17 at 08:02 -0700, Nidayatou Ayeva wrote:
> Hello,
>
>
> I am conducting an ecological study on the association between breast cancer
> incidence and social deprivation (Fdep). The incidence variable follows a
> Poisson distribution. The relationship appears to be non-linear, and I would
